"cli.usage" = "Usage: proctor <command> [options]\n\nWatches coding agents working in worktrees and tells you when one raises its hand.\n\n  ls             list the agents that are running\n                   --all              cover every repository\n                   --json             print JSON (for AI and the sidebar)\n  worktree ls    list the worktrees, running or not\n                   --all              cover every repository\n                   --json             print JSON (for AI)\n  skill [NAME]   print a procedure for your agent to follow (no name lists them)\n  setup [AGENT]  print how to wire proctor up (no name lists the agents)\n  attach <ID>    open that session's agent (claude / agy / codex), resuming it\n  rm <ID>        drop one entry from the ledger (the worktree is left alone)\n  sidebar        launch the sidebar that clings to iTerm2 (Agent Proctor.app)\n  --version      print the version\n\nIt neither creates nor cleans up worktrees itself. It shows what is there, and\n`skill worktree` hands your agent the procedure for the rest.";

